{
  "about": "Every recorded sound the game ships, as a recipe: where it comes from (the sound's own page, whose licence tools/sounds/build.py checks) and how to cut it. `loop`: seconds of the steadiest stretch (or `at` [start, end]), crossfaded so it loops. `shots`: how many separate events to cut (the loudest ones, each at most `max` seconds), saved as name-1, name-2... `hp`/`lp`: filter (Hz). `chunks`/`len`: that many stretches of `len` seconds where it's loudest, for sounds that never stop. Run `python3 tools/sounds/build.py` after changing it.",
